'''HDFC Bank Limited''' is an Indian [[banking]] and [[financial services]] company headquartered in [[Mumbai]]. Incorporated in August 1994, it officially commenced operations in January 1995 upon receiving its banking license from Reserve Bank of India.<ref name=":0">https://www.hdfc.bank.in/content/dam/hdfcbankpws/in/en/personal-banking/discover-products/about-us/who-we-are/pdfs/milestones.pdf</ref> It is India's largest private sector bank by assets and market capitalisation.<ref>{{cite web |title=Top companies in India by total assets |url=https://www.moneycontrol.com/stocks/marketinfo/totassets/bse/bank-private.html |publisher=Moneycontrol |access-date=10 January 2025}}</ref> In 2025 HDFC became the 10th largest bank in the world by market capitalisation.<ref>{{Cite web |date=2025-05-02 |title=Top 10 largest banks in the world by market cap (2025): Indian bank in the global 10 |url=https://indianexpress.com/article/trending/top-10-listing/top-10-largest-banks-in-the-world-by-market-cap-2025-9978985/ |access-date=2025-10-23 |website=The Indian Express |language=en}}</ref> As of 2026, HDFC is the first out of the 10 most valuable banks in India.<ref>{{Cite web |date=2026-04-11 |title=Top 10 most valuable banks in India in 2026: SBI overtakes ICICI Bank in market cap to become #2, check who is #1 |url=https://indianexpress.com/article/trending/top-10-listing/top-10-most-valuable-banks-in-india-in-2026-10631398/ |access-date=2026-07-14 |website=The Indian Express |language=en}}</ref>

The [[Reserve Bank of India]] (RBI) has identified the HDFC Bank, [[State Bank of India]], and [[ICICI Bank]] as [[Systemically important financial institution|Domestic Systemically Important Banks]] (D-SIBs), which are often referred to as banks that are “[[too big to fail]]”.<ref>{{cite web |url=https://rbi.org.in/Scripts/BS_PressReleaseDisplay.aspx?prid=54979 |title=RBI releases 2022 list of Domestic Systemically Important Banks (D-SIBs) |date=2 January 2023 |website=rbi.org.in |publisher=RBI |access-date=6 December 2023 |quote=State Bank of India, ICICI Bank, and HDFC Bank continue to be identified as Domestic Systemically Important Banks (D-SIBs), under the same bucketing structure as in the 2021 list of D-SIBs.}}</ref><ref>{{cite news |last= |first= |date=2 January 2023 |title=RBI releases Domestic Systemically Important Banks (D-SIBs) of 2022 |url=https://www.livemint.com/news/india/rbi-releases-domestic-systemically-important-banks-d-sibs-of-2021-list-here-11672660568619.html |work=Livemint |location=New Delhi |access-date=6 December 2023}}</ref>

[[File:EXCON 2025, Bangalore International Exhibition Centre (396).jpg|thumb|right|HDFC Bank at [[EXCON]] 2025, [[Bangalore International Exhibition Centre|BIEC]]]]

As of April 2026, HDFC Bank has a market capitalization of  $137.15 billion.<ref>{{Cite web |date=2026-04-11 |title=Top 10 most valuable banks in India in 2026: SBI overtakes ICICI Bank in market cap to become #2, check who is #1 |url=https://indianexpress.com/article/trending/top-10-listing/top-10-most-valuable-banks-in-india-in-2026-10631398/ |access-date=2026-07-14 |website=The Indian Express |language=en}}</ref> And as of April 2024, HDFC Bank has a market capitalization of $145 billion making it the third-largest company on the [[Indian stock exchange|Indian stock exchanges]].<ref>{{Cite web|url=http://www.moneycontrol.com/stocks/marketinfo/marketcap/bse/banks-private-sector.html|title=Largest bank by Market capitalization|website=MoneyControl|access-date=1 October 2014|archive-date=6 June 2021|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20210606043759/https://www.moneycontrol.com/stocks/marketinfo/marketcap/bse/banks-private-sector.html|url-status=live}}</ref> In 2023, it was the [[List of largest employers in India|sixteenth largest employer in India]] with over 173,000 employees, after its [[takeover]] of parent company [[Housing Development Finance Corporation]].<ref>{{Cite web |title= Financial Results (Indian GAAP) for the Quarter and Year Ended March 31, 2023 |url=https://www.hdfcbank.com/content/bbp/repositories/723fb80a-2dde-42a3-9793-7ae1be57c87f/?path=/Footer/About%20Us/Investor%20Relation/Detail%20PAges/financial%20results/PDFs/2023/Press-Release-March-2023.pdf|date= 31 March 2023 |website= hdfcbank.com |publisher= HDFC Bank |access-date= 16 November 2023 |page= 4}}</ref><ref>{{Cite web|url=https://www.macrotrends.net/stocks/charts/HDB/hdfc-bank/number-of-employees|title=HDFC Bank: Number of Employees 2006–2021 &#124; HDB|website=macrotrends.net|access-date=22 May 2021|archive-date=22 May 2021|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20210522071805/https://www.macrotrends.net/stocks/charts/HDB/hdfc-bank/number-of-employees|url-status=live}}</ref>

== History ==
HDFC Bank was incorporated in 1994 as a subsidiary of [[Housing Development Finance Corporation|HDFC Ltd]], under the leadership of [[Deepak Parekh]], nephew of HDFC Ltd's founder H.T Parekh. the parent company. which received an 'in principle' approval from the RBI to set up a bank in the Private Sector as part of its [[Economic liberalisation in India|liberalisation]] of the Indian banking industry.<ref>{{cite web |url=https://www.hdfcbank.com/personal/about-us/overview/who-we-are |title=About HDFC Bank |website=hdfcbank.com |publisher=HDFC Bank |access-date=6 December 2023}}</ref><ref>{{cite web |url=https://www.careratings.com/upload/CompanyFiles/PR/202305140546_HDFC_Bank_Ltd.pdf |title=HDFC Bank Ltd |date=2 May 2023 |website=careratings.com |publisher=CARE Ratings |access-date=6 December 2023 |quote=The Housing Development Finance Corporation Limited (HDFC) was among the first institutions to receive an 'in principle' approval from RBI to set up a bank in the private sector, as part of the RBI's liberalization of the Indian banking industry in 1994. The bank was incorporated in August 1994 in the name of 'HDFC Bank Limited' (HBL), with its registered office in Mumbai, India.}}</ref> [[Aditya Puri]] was appointed as its first managing director to lead the newly formed institution.<ref>{{cite news |last=Bhattacharya |first=Tamal |title=The Making of HDFC Bank: Aditya Puri and the Legacy |url=https://www.business-standard.com |publisher=Business Standard |date=26 October 2020 |access-date=2 July 2026}}</ref> The bank commenced operations in January 1995, with its registered office in [[Mumbai]].<ref>{{Cite web|url=http://profit.ndtv.com/stock/hdfc-bank-ltd_hdfcbank/reports|title=HDFC Bank: Reports, Company History, Directors Report, Chairman's Speech, Auditors Report of HDFC Bank|website=profit.ndtv.com|access-date=16 July 2016|archive-date=9 July 2016|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20160709001214/http://profit.ndtv.com/stock/hdfc-bank-ltd_hdfcbank/reports|url-status=live}}</ref> Its first corporate office and a full-service branch at Sandoz House, [[Worli]], was inaugurated by the then [[Ministry of Finance (India)|Union Finance Minister]], [[Manmohan Singh]].<ref>{{cite news |title=HDFC Bank to shift HQ from where it had started its operations 25 years ago |url=https://www.business-standard.com/article/finance/hdfc-bank-to-shift-hq-from-where-it-had-started-its-operations-25-years-ago-119110601671_1.html |access-date=20 April 2026 |work=Business Standard}}</ref>

In 1999, HDFC Bank merged with Times Bank, marking the first friendly merger and share-swap deal in the Indian banking sector.<ref name=":0" />

In 2000, HDFC Bank became the first bank in India to introduce mobile banking, offering SMS-based services for account management and transaction requests.<ref name=":0" />

In July 2001, HDFC Bank's [[American depository receipt|ADS]] listed on the [[New York Stock Exchange]] after an IPO.<ref>{{cite news |title=HDFC Bank prices ADS at $13.83: Reuters |url=https://www.rediff.com/money/2001/jul/20hdfc1.htm |access-date=8 May 2024 |work=Rediff.com}}</ref>

In 2008, HDFC Bank acquired the [[Centurion Bank of Punjab]] (CBoP) for {{INRconvert|9510|c|mode=historical|lk=c|year=2008}} in a [[Stock swap|share-swap]] deal, reportedly the largest acquisition in the Indian financial sector at the time.<ref>{{cite news |title=HDFC Bank buys Centurion in India's biggest financial sector buyout |url=https://www.nytimes.com/2008/02/24/business/worldbusiness/24iht-indiabank24.10327786.html |access-date=8 May 2024 |work=The New York Times |date=4 December 2008}}</ref>

In 2015, as part of its "Go Digital" campaign HDFC Bank introduced the digital payment solutions PayZapp and Chillr to facilitate mobile payments, transfers, and shopping.<ref name=":0" />

In August 2017, the bank set up an in-house Digital Command centre (DCC) to track customer interaction and brand sentiment across social media platforms.<ref name=":0" />

In October 2020, Sashidhar Jagdishan was appointed as Managing Director and CEO of HDFC Bank for a three-year term following RBI approval.<ref name=":0" />

In 2021, the bank acquired a 9.99% stake in Ferbine, an entity promoted by [[Tata Group]], to operate a pan-India umbrella entity for retail payment systems, similar to the [[National Payments Corporation of India]].<ref>{{Cite web|title=Kotak Mahindra Bank, HDFC Bank To Acquire 9.99% Each In Ferbine|url=https://www.moneycontrol.com/news/business/markets/kotak-mahindra-bank-hdfc-bank-to-acquire-9-99-each-in-ferbine-private-ltd-6578201.html|access-date=4 March 2021|website=Moneycontrol|date=26 February 2021 |archive-date=14 April 2021|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20210414103152/https://www.moneycontrol.com/news/business/markets/kotak-mahindra-bank-hdfc-bank-to-acquire-9-99-each-in-ferbine-private-ltd-6578201.html|url-status=live}}</ref> 

In December 2021, HDFC Bank partnered with Indian Post Payments Bank to distribute banking services across rural and semi-urban location.<ref name=":0" />

In 2021, HDFC Bank entered into a partnership with Paytm to issue co-branded Visa credit cards for retail customers and business merchants.<ref name=":0" />

In 2022, HDFC Bank provided financing for a 550-tonne per-day municipal waste to biogas plant in Indore, operated by Indore Clean Energy.<ref name=":0" />

Following approval from the Reserve Bank of India on 19 April 2023, HDFC Bank appointed Kaizad Bharucha as Deputy Managing Director and Bhavesh Zaveri as Executive Director, both serving three-year terms.<ref name=":0" />

=== HDFC Ltd–HDFC Bank merger ===
On 4 April 2022, [[Housing Development Finance Corporation|HDFC Ltd]] announced that it would merge with HDFC Bank, marking India's largest-ever [[Mergers and acquisitions|M&A deal]].<ref>{{Cite news|url=https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/business/india-business/hdfc-to-merge-with-hdfc-bank-in-indias-biggest-ever-ma/articleshow/90651390.cms|title = HDFC HDFC Bank Merger: HDFC to merge with HDFC Bank in India's biggest-ever M&A &#124; |website = [[The Times of India]]| date=5 April 2022 }}</ref><ref name="bloomberg_0623">{{cite news |last1=Singh |first1=Preeti |last2=Patil |first2=Divya |title=Bank Giant Bigger Than Morgan Stanley Arises From India Merger |url=https://www.bloomberg.com/news/articles/2023-06-30/india-s-hdfc-vaults-into-ranks-of-world-s-most-valuable-banks?fromMostRead=true&sref=CIpmV6x8 |work=Bloomberg.com |date=30 June 2023 |language=en}}</ref> As part of the merger, HDFC Ltd would transfer its [[mortgage|home loan]] portfolio to HDFC Bank, while the bank offered depositors of HDFC Ltd the choice of either withdrawing their money or renewing their deposits with the bank at the [[interest rate]] that the bank was then offering.<ref>{{Cite news |last=Kulkarni |first=Sneha |date=3 July 2023 |title=What is the HDFC Bank-HDFC merger date |work=The Economic Times |url=https://economictimes.indiatimes.com/wealth/save/what-is-the-hdfc-bank-hdfc-merger-date/articleshow/101414476.cms |access-date=4 July 2023 |issn=0013-0389}}</ref>

On 1 July 2023, the merger of HDFC Ltd with HDFC Bank was completed.<ref name="hd4">{{cite news |title=HDFC Bank completes merger with HDFC after final board approval |url=https://economictimes.indiatimes.com/industry/banking/finance/banking/hdfc-bank-completes-merger-with-hdfc-after-final-board-approval/articleshow/101402111.cms |access-date=27 December 2023 |publisher=The Economic Times |date=1 July 2023}}</ref><ref name="hd3">{{cite news |last1=Mishra |first1=Lalatendu |title=HDFC Bank completes merger formalities, rebrands HDFC Ltd. offices, branches |url=https://www.thehindu.com/business/Industry/hdfc-bank-completes-merger-formalities-rebrands-hdfc-ltd-offices-branches/article67030718.ece |access-date=27 December 2023 |work=The Hindu |date=1 July 2023 |language=en-IN}}</ref> Consequently, HDFC Bank had a [[Market capitalization|market capitalisation]] of $154 billion, becoming the seventh most valuable bank in the world. HDFC Bank also became one of the [[List of largest banks|world's top 100 banking companies]] by total assets.<ref name="hd1">{{cite news |title=HDFC Ltd-HDFC Bank merger: Behind Sashi Jagdishan's big plans for HDFC Bank |url=https://www.businesstoday.in/magazine/the-buzz/story/hdfc-ltd-hdfc-bank-merger-behind-sashi-jagdishans-big-plans-for-hdfc-bank-390643-2023-07-20 |access-date=27 December 2023 |publisher=Business Today |date=20 July 2023 |language=en}}</ref><ref name="hd2">{{cite news |last1=Mascarenhas |first1=Rajesh |title=HDFC Bank becomes world's 7th largest lender post merger |url=https://economictimes.indiatimes.com/markets/stocks/news/hdfc-bank-becomes-worlds-7th-largest-lender-post-merger/articleshow/101840225.cms |access-date=27 December 2023 |publisher=The Economic Times |date=18 July 2023}}</ref>

The combined entity had a customer base of 12 crore (120 million), surpassing the population of Germany in size.<ref name="hd5">{{cite news |date=30 June 2023 |title=Bank giant bigger than Morgan Stanley arises from HDFC Bank, HDFC Ltd merger |url=https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/business/india-business/bank-giant-bigger-than-morgan-stanley-arises-from-hdfc-bank-hdfc-ltd-merger/articleshow/101380691.cms?from=mdr |access-date=27 December 2023 |work=The Times of India}}</ref> The merger resulted in a substantial increase in bank headcount, with the workforce totaling 1.77 lakh (177k) employees. The merged entity became the second-largest bank in India, trailing only the [[State Bank of India]] in terms of assets.<ref name="hd8">{{cite news |date=3 July 2023 |title=Spotlight on HDFC Ltd and HDFC Bank Merger ! |url=https://www.cnbctv18.com/business/companies/hdfc-ltd-and-hdfc-bank-merger-record-date-ftse-nifty-sensex-msci-mutual-funds-17103621.htm |access-date=27 December 2023 |publisher=CNBCTV18 |language=en}}</ref> The number of branches increased to 8,300.<ref name="hd6">{{cite news |date=1 July 2023 |title=HDFC Ltd and HDFC Bank complete their merger today: Take a look at what's happened so far |url=https://www.zeebiz.com/personal-finance/banking/news-hdfc-ltd-completes-its-merger-with-and-hdfc-bank-today-sashidhar-jagdishan-home-loans-nse-bse-242387 |access-date=27 December 2023 |publisher=Zee Business}}</ref>

Shares of HDFC Ltd were delisted and shareholders were allotted 42 shares of HDFC Bank for every 25 shares of HDFC Ltd held,<ref name="hd9">{{cite news |title=HDFC-HDFC Bank merger likely to be effective July 1, HDFC to be delisted on July 13: Deepak Parekh |url=https://www.businesstoday.in/industry/banks/story/hdfc-hdfc-bank-merger-to-be-effective-july-1-hdfc-to-be-delisted-july-13-deepak-parekh-387245-2023-06-27 |access-date=27 December 2023 |publisher=Business Today |date=27 June 2023 |language=en}}</ref> leading to an increase in the equity capital of HDFC Bank.<ref name="hd7">{{cite news |last1=Tan |first1=Charmaine Jacob, Joanna |title=India's HDFC Bank completes $40 billion takeover of the country's largest mortgage lender. Here's what it means |url=https://www.cnbc.com/2023/07/03/indias-hdfc-bank-completes-40-billion-merger-with-mortgage-lender-hdfc.html |access-date=27 December 2023 |publisher=CNBC |date=3 July 2023 |language=en}}</ref>

By March 2025, this bank reported a 5.4% increase in year-on-year (YoY) surge in its advances to ₹28.2 lakh crore.<ref>{{Cite web |title=HDFC Bank confident of growing advances on par with industry in 2025-26 fiscal year |url=https://upstox.com/news/market-news/stocks/hdfc-bank-confident-of-growing-advances-on-par-with-industry-in-2025-26-fiscal-year/article-178051/ |access-date=2026-07-14 |website=upstox.com |language=en}}</ref> During this time period (of FY25), the bank reflected the results of the first full year of operation since the merger on July 1, 2023. <ref>{{Cite web |title=HDFC Bank confident of growing advances on par with industry in 2025-26 fiscal year |url=https://upstox.com/news/market-news/stocks/hdfc-bank-confident-of-growing-advances-on-par-with-industry-in-2025-26-fiscal-year/article-178051/ |access-date=2026-07-14 |website=upstox.com |language=en}}</ref> Post the merger, the bank was able to keep a healthy growth, all while maintaining asset quality. <ref>{{Cite web |title=HDFC Bank confident of growing advances on par with industry in 2025-26 fiscal year |url=https://upstox.com/news/market-news/stocks/hdfc-bank-confident-of-growing-advances-on-par-with-industry-in-2025-26-fiscal-year/article-178051/ |access-date=2026-07-14 |website=upstox.com |language=en}}</ref> A net profit of ₹67,347.4 during the March FY25 quarter, increasing YoY by 10.7% and the net interest income grew by 13%. <ref>{{Cite web |title=HDFC Bank confident of growing advances on par with industry in 2025-26 fiscal year |url=https://upstox.com/news/market-news/stocks/hdfc-bank-confident-of-growing-advances-on-par-with-industry-in-2025-26-fiscal-year/article-178051/ |access-date=2026-07-14 |website=upstox.com |language=en}}</ref>

== Operations ==
[[File:HDFC Bank.jpg|thumb|A branch of HDFC Bank in [[Hyderabad]]]]
As of June 30,2026, HDFC Bank's distribution network included 9,694 branches and 20,958 ATMs (cash recyclers; cash deposit and withdrawal) spread throughout 4,175 cities and villages.<ref name=":1">https://www.hdfc.bank.in/about-us/who-we-are</ref>

HDFC Bank is the sole private bank operating in the union territory of [[Lakshadweep]] after opening a branch in [[Kavaratti]] island.<ref>{{Cite web |date=10 April 2024 |title=Sole Private Bank Operator in UT Lakshdweep |url=https://indianexpress.com/article/business/hdfc-bank-first-private-bank-brach-office-in-lakshadweep-kavaratti-9261984/ |access-date=12 April 2024 |website=The Indian Express}}</ref>

The Bank's international operations comprises five branches, located in Bahrain, Dubai, Hong Kong and Singapore and an IFSC Banking Unit in Gujarat International Finance Tec-City. Additionally, it has four representative offices in Abu Dhabi, Dubai, London and Nairobi respectively.<ref name=":1" />

== Employees ==
During the FY26 quarter, the bank reduced its workforce by 3343 employees. The total workforce of the bank reduced from 2,14,521 to 2,11,178, by March 2026. This mainly targeted non-supervisory roles, and the number of workmen, clerical and subordinate staff reduced from 1,70,950 in FY25 to 1,62,797 in FY26. <ref>{{Cite web |last=Goel |first=Sheetal |date=2026-07-13 |title=HDFC Bank trims workforce by over 3,300 in FY26, says tech will elevate, not replace people {{!}} Company Business News |url=https://www.livemint.com/companies/people/hdfc-bank-trims-workforce-by-over-3-300-in-fy26-says-tech-will-elevate-not-replace-people-11783920020535.html |access-date=2026-07-14 |website=mint |language=en}}</ref>

The top voices of the bank opined that this was to elevate the experience of banking by combining human experience with technological innovation, by automating operations via technology. By integrating AI with HR digital solutions, the processes will be simplified, self-services will be made prominent, and a seamless employee journey would be ensured. This technology-led transformation was backed by the Managing Director and CEO of the bank, [[Sashidhar Jagdishan]], who opined that the employees must evolve alongside the organisation.<ref>{{Cite web |last=Goel |first=Sheetal |date=2026-07-13 |title=HDFC Bank trims workforce by over 3,300 in FY26, says tech will elevate, not replace people {{!}} Company Business News |url=https://www.livemint.com/companies/people/hdfc-bank-trims-workforce-by-over-3-300-in-fy26-says-tech-will-elevate-not-replace-people-11783920020535.html |access-date=2026-07-14 |website=mint |language=en}}</ref> The employees were supported for technological upskilling; around 50,631 employees were trained through the bank's GenAI Academy and other AI programmes. Around twenty thousand employees were also trained in [[Microsoft Copilot]] training. <ref>{{Cite web |last=www.ETBFSI.com |title=HDFC Bank cuts non supervisory workforce by over 8,000 in FY26, ramps up management hiring |url=https://bfsi.economictimes.indiatimes.com/articles/hdfc-bank-streamlines-workforce-by-reducing-8000-non-supervisory-jobs-while-increasing-management-roles/132329042 |access-date=2026-07-14 |website=ETBFSI.com |language=en}}</ref>

Though the total workforce saw a decline, there was an increase in the management roles. Multiple employees were welcomed into senior, middle-management and junior management roles- about a 1000 employees were welcomed into middle-management roles, while junior management roles saw an increase by 3000 employees. <ref>{{Cite web |last=Goel |first=Sheetal |date=2026-07-13 |title=HDFC Bank trims workforce by over 3,300 in FY26, says tech will elevate, not replace people {{!}} Company Business News |url=https://www.livemint.com/companies/people/hdfc-bank-trims-workforce-by-over-3-300-in-fy26-says-tech-will-elevate-not-replace-people-11783920020535.html |access-date=2026-07-14 |website=mint |language=en}}</ref>

FY26 showed significant changes in diversity metrics as well. 27% of the workforce was women - the representation of women in STEM roles amounted to 27% and the women in management roles occupied 16% of the total roles. <ref>{{Cite web |last=www.ETBFSI.com |title=HDFC Bank cuts non supervisory workforce by over 8,000 in FY26, ramps up management hiring |url=https://bfsi.economictimes.indiatimes.com/articles/hdfc-bank-streamlines-workforce-by-reducing-8000-non-supervisory-jobs-while-increasing-management-roles/132329042 |access-date=2026-07-14 |website=ETBFSI.com |language=en}}</ref>

